<h2 align="center">Learn More about TMS Therapy</h2>
<div class="wp-caption alignright" id="attachment_406" style="width: 460px"><img alt="" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-406" class="size-full wp-image-406" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 784px) 100vw, 784px" data-lazy-src="/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/normal-vs-depressed-brain.jpg" data-lazy-srcset="/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/normal-vs-depressed-brain.jpg 784w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/04/normal-vs-depressed-brain-300x208.jpg 300w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/04/normal-vs-depressed-brain-768x533.jpg 768w" decoding="async" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20450%200'%3E%3C/svg%3E" width="450"/><noscript><img alt="" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-406" class="size-full wp-image-406" decoding="async" sizes="(max-width: 784px) 100vw, 784px" src="/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/normal-vs-depressed-brain.jpg" srcset="/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/normal-vs-depressed-brain.jpg 784w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/04/normal-vs-depressed-brain-300x208.jpg 300w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/04/normal-vs-depressed-brain-768x533.jpg 768w" width="450"/></noscript><p class="wp-caption-text" id="caption-attachment-406">TMS targets areas of the brain affected by depression to improve functioning</p></div>
<p>TMS uses non-invasive technology to improve electrical functioning of neurons. Approximately 50-60% of patients report significant relief of their depressive symptoms, whereas around 30-40% of people report complete resolution of their depression.</p>
<p><strong>TMS Therapy is:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Virtually side effect free</li>
<li>Non-invasive</li>
<li>Medication free</li>
<li>Covered by most insurances &amp; Medicare</li>
<li>FDA approved</li>
<li>If you are struggling, there is hope. We can help.</li>
</ul>
<p><a class="btn" href="/tms-therapy/">Learn More</a></p>
